hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15622","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Imran, meaning al-Qattan, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi, from Muawiyah al-Laythi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People will be in drought, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will send down upon them provision from His provision, and in the morning they become polytheists. It was said to him: How is that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They say: we were rained by such and such star."
